From 1e1cb0d7c94f09b862f99db9739ac22867100a87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 01:01:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mt-mcp-tenant-scope: scope MCPManager name collision by
 tenant id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The MCPManager's clientMap is keyed by client ID (UUID, never
collides) but its name-collision check at clientmanager.go:99 uses
GetClientByName() which iterates the entire map matching only on
ExecutionConfig.Name. In MT mode that's a global collision: two
tenants both choosing 'isotest_echo' fight, and the second create
fails — isolation test I6.

Patch16 (Option A) tenant-scopes the collision check without
introducing per-tenant MCPManager instances:

  - core/schemas/mcp.go: add TenantID to MCPClientConfig (JSON tag
    '-' so the wire shape stays upstream-compatible) and to the
    in-memory MCPClientState.
  - core/mcp/utils.go: GetClientByName signature becomes
    (tenantID, clientName string). Empty tenantID falls back to
    'any tenant' so OSS single-tenant and CodeMode call sites
    (which don't carry tenant context at script level) keep working.
  - core/mcp/{clientmanager,mcp}.go: AddClient and the bootstrap
    fallback stamp TenantID from the incoming config onto the new
    MCPClientState.
  - All call sites updated: toolmanager.go + agent.go read tenant
    from BifrostContext via TenantIDFromBifrostContext; CodeMode
    Starlark sites pass '' (any-tenant, fine because script
    execution is already tenant-routed at a higher layer).
  - framework/configstore/rdb.go: three configstore-to-schema
    conversions propagate dbClient.TenantID into
    MCPClientConfig.TenantID.
  - transports/bifrost-http/handlers/mcp.go: createMCPClient and
    its OAuth pending-config sibling stamp TenantID from
    TenantIDFromCtx(ctx), so the runtime AddMCPClient call (which
    routes through the singleton MCPManager today) reaches the
    tenant-scoped collision check.

Ships with unit tests at core/mcp/utils_tenant_scope_test.go
(TestGetClientByName_TenantScope, TestGetClientByName_CrossTenantNoLeak)
that lock the invariant directly at the choke point. Flips I6 in
examples/isolation/main.go from RED to GREEN.

Trade-offs called out in the design: tool servers, health monitors,
toolSyncManager, the in-process MCP server, and the OAuth provider
remain process-globals — so a misbehaving STDIO subprocess in
tenant A's MCP client still affects everyone. The next patch in
this lane (call it 1B-extended / Option B in plan notes) would
build per-tenant MCPManager instances at TenantLoader time,
giving each tenant isolated local servers and monitors. That's a
larger lift (TenantLoader builds a tenant-filtered MCPConfig +
bifrost.Init wires it). Tracked for after the current series
quiets down.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
